**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1061 onwards, standing assumption**

a Brownian motion starts at 0, has continuous paths, and
   Gaussian independent increments. We use Mathlib's `IsBrownianReal`
   (time indexed by `ℝ≥0`).


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1062, display after (1.1) / expectations of the form E[f(∫ e^{σW+νs} ds)]**

the integral of exponential Brownian motion with drift up to time t.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1061, joint law in (1.1)**

the law of the pair (∫₀ᵗ e^{σW_s+νs} ds, W_t).


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1061, (1.1), φ_{t,σ}(x,y)**

φ is a Lebesgue density of that joint law.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1065, Prop. 2.2 factorization**

the conditional density φ(x|y) of the integral given W_t = y,
   related by φ(x,y) = gaussianPDF(y) · φ(x|y).


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1061 (1.1) — Yor’s theorem [33, (6.c)]**

stated here; proved in `IntegralReps` as `yor_formula` via Remark 5.1.
   Definitions `theta` and `yorDensity` live in `Lyasoff2016.Theta` / `Lyasoff2016.YorDensity`.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1062, densities of the form (1.2)**

inverse-Gamma shape densities a^{p-1}/Γ(p-1) · x^{-p} e^{-a/x}.


**Lyasoff (2016), p. 1063, display (1.3)**

time-reversibility in law for integral functionals of BM:
   (∫ V_i(s,W_s) ds, W_t) has the same law as (∫ V_i(t-s, W_t-W_s) ds, W_t).
